
# Divider: the vocabulary's word for a line between things (note/term/view/11-vocabulary.md). No props: a hairline
# across its stack, horizontal in a column and vertical in a row, which every host decides from the stack it lands in.
# Drawn as an `hr` on the DOM and as a one point view in the platform's separator color by every toolkit
# (test/compile/toolkit-words.ts). Its color is the look sheet's.
#
# It replaces ./separator.tree (the shadcn port: a `div` with an orientation prop), shelved with `note draft`.

load @term/site/code/dom/dom
  find view

view divider
  take host, like view
  view hr
    bind data-slot, text <divider>
